{"correction_of": "F0047 receipt, unit U-0003-SEQ", "file_id": "F0047", "status": "VOID — ADMITTED BUT NOT READ", "when": "2026-09-23", "why": "The receipt was issued at admission and the session was stopped before the file was opened. Its field name is sha256_at_read, which would assert a read that did not occur. Voided rather than deleted: the earlier record stands and this annotates it.", "rule_applied": "A receipt must never assert a binding that did not happen — the same rule that forbade backfilling receipts for the first 40 files.", "instrument_defect_noted": "⚠️ admit.py --receipt performs admission AND writes a read receipt in one step, so a receipt can exist for a file that was never opened. Recorded as an observation; the instrument is not changed here."}
